-- REM-A7-OWNER-B-1 (2026-10-26, remediation agent rem-a7; charter pillars cost, autonomy, security; agent_issues 100384, 100406, 1000063, 1000068, 1000079).
-- Owner-queue investigations answered with measured findings, each closed only on its own evidence and with the work that remains filed as an issue with a doer and a failing probe:
--   * 100384 and 100406 (owner-local desktop spend, 30 day breakdown, tagging, the 300 dollar all-in recommendation): the attribution is delivered; a per-client split is not possible without a client-side tag, and the tag the
--     fleet's own ingest knows (worker or caller) would move the spend into the fleet caps, so the successor OWNER-LOCAL-CLIENT-TAG-1 teaches the ingest a separate key (owner_client) and a card asks the owner
--     to set it on his own machines (IDENTITY-BOUND). The table the successor writes, ai_spend_owner_client, is created here.
--   * 1000063 (five unowned items of the audit thread): each of the five now has a measured disposition (two resolved, one per-owner triage with its machinery, one denominator explained, one source pinned).
--   * 1000068 (security and compliance review of the research and content area): ranked findings with the smallest fix for the worst one and an owner for each; one new issue for the consent-violation ledger.
--   * 1000079 (qnfo-code-orchestrator internalError): diagnosed to the class (a stalled scheduled invocation, 13 in 24 hours at the 15 minute wall limit and almost no CPU) and handed to the code loop as
--     CODE-ORCH-WALL-STALL-1 with a bounded first lever and a probe that fails today.
-- A card that has a stated default is closed at birth by the trigger human_actions_default_adopt_ai (it did so to the Search Console card of REM-A7-REACH-1): the card written here is reopened in the next statement, and
-- so is attest-first-credibility-event of REM-A7-OWNER-A-1, which the trigger closed at birth on 2026-10-26 (human_actions 190) because the reopen statement of that file was pushed after the pull request merged.
-- A new issue's contract is born superseded with the generic template, so each successor's contract is set to its measuring probe in this same file.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE agent_issues SET status = 'open', close_channel = NULL, updated_at = CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE id IN (100384, 100406, 1000063, 1000068, 1000079) AND close_channel = 'auto:triage-sync:rem-a7'; UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = 'triaged' WHERE issue_id IN (100384, 100406, 1000063, 1000068, 1000079) AND rc = 'rem-a7-owner-b'; UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = 'closed', owner = 'rem-a7', close_evidence = 'rolled back with migrations/2026-10-26-rem-a7-owner-b.sql' WHERE issue_id IN (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'OWNER-LOCAL-CLIENT-TAG-1:%' OR title LIKE 'CODE-ORCH-WALL-STALL-1:%' OR title LIKE 'EMAIL-OWNER-CODE-VIOLATION-NOISE-1:%'); UPDATE human_actions SET status = 'resolved', resolution = 'rolled back with migrations/2026-10-26-rem-a7-owner-b.sql' WHERE slug IN ('tag-owner-desktop-clients', 'attest-first-credibility-event')

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ai_spend_owner_client (
  day TEXT NOT NULL, gateway TEXT NOT NULL, provider TEXT NOT NULL, model TEXT NOT NULL, client TEXT NOT NULL,
  calls INTEGER DEFAULT 0, in_tok INTEGER DEFAULT 0, out_tok INTEGER DEFAULT 0, usd REAL DEFAULT 0,
  PRIMARY KEY (day, gateway, provider, model, client)
);

INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT
  'OWNER-LOCAL-CLIENT-TAG-1: owner-local desktop spend (242.43 USD in 30 days) cannot be split by client; the gateway log carries no tag and the fleet tag would move it into the fleet caps',
  'Charter pillar: cost. Found closing the owner audit tasks 100384 and 100406, measured 2026-10-26 in qnfo-audit.ai_spend_owner_local and on the AI Gateway log (cf-ops-actions gateway-logs runs 40383249752 and 40383253899, non-content fields).' || char(10) ||
  'PROBLEM: every owner-local request carries user_agent node, the account''s gateway token, the stored provider key and no metadata, so two desktop clients of the same person look alike and the owner''s question (which client costs what) has no answer. 30 day list cost 242.43 USD: claude-opus-5.5 177.57 (1,802 calls on 3 days), claude-sonnet-5.5 33.05, deepseek-flash 23.17, deepseek-v4-pro 8.64.' || char(10) ||
  'WHY NOT THE EXISTING TAG: qnfo-fleet-control olClassify takes any request whose metadata has worker or caller as fleet spend (ai_spend_ledger under that name, counted against fleet_budget ai_spend:anthropic cap 15 and ai_spend:total cap 150), so tagging a desktop client the way a fleet worker is tagged would move about 242 USD of owner list cost into the fleet caps. One AI Gateway per client is ruled out by fleet_budget ai_gateways cap 1.' || char(10) ||
  'FIX (qnfo-fleet-control/worker.js only; the table ai_spend_owner_client was created by migrations/2026-10-26-rem-a7-owner-b.sql): in olClassify a request whose metadata carries owner_client (a string up to 40 characters) stays owner-local and its client name is returned with the classification; ownerLocalIngest also upserts day, gateway, provider, model, client, calls, in_tok, out_tok and usd into ai_spend_owner_client. ai_spend_owner_local is written exactly as before, so every existing reader and total is unchanged; a request with worker or caller and no owner_client behaves as today.' || char(10) ||
  'Definition of done: qnfo-fleet-control on main carries the owner_client handling and, once the owner has tagged a client (card tag-owner-desktop-clients, IDENTITY-BOUND: the client settings are on his own machines), SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ai_spend_owner_client WHERE day >= date(''now'', ''-7 days'') reads 1 or more.' || char(10) ||
  'code-probe: {"paths": ["qnfo-fleet-control/worker.js"], "contains": "ai_spend_owner_client"}' || char(10) ||
  'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-fleet-control/worker.js' || char(10) ||
  'code-anchor: if (!w) return { kind: "owner-local", caller: "owner-local" };',
  'claude-session:rem-a7', 'ops', 'medium', 'open',
  CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'OWNER-LOCAL-CLIENT-TAG-1:%' AND status = 'open');

INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT
  'CODE-ORCH-WALL-STALL-1: qnfo-code-orchestrator scheduled invocations stall at the 15 minute wall limit with almost no CPU (13 in 24 hours, 71 in 7 days)',
  'Charter pillar: autonomy. Diagnosis of owner task 1000079 (qnfo-code-orchestrator internalError), measured 2026-10-26 in qnfo-audit.worker_logs (Logpush failures) and worker_usage_daily.' || char(10) ||
  'FINDING: the worker''s scheduled invocations stall. 13 invocations in the last 24 hours and 71 in 7 days ran 899.7 to 900.0 seconds of wall time (the 15 minute cron limit) with at most 200 ms of CPU and ended canceled or exceededWallTime (today at 16:59:44Z, 16:53:44Z, 16:03:44Z, 06:57:44Z, 06:37:44Z). CPU time says the handler was not working: it was awaiting something that never returned. Separately 120 exception rows in 7 days (about 60 events, each logged twice) carry the platform codes 3046 Request timeout and 5030 with no cpu or wall time: the owner''s count of 3 events is the census figure of those (worker_usage_daily errors_24h 4 of 1,366 requests on 10-24, 6 of 1,869 today); they are platform-side, not thrown by this code. The stalls do not track a deploy: 0.28.0 went live 2026-10-26T06:24Z and they continue at 06:37, 06:57, 16:03, 16:53 and 16:59.' || char(10) ||
  'WHERE (read in qnfo-code-orchestrator/worker.js on main, not proven): scheduled() awaits runFleetExecMember (the folded fleet-exec member) and hands the main tick to ctx.waitUntil. Unbounded waits on that path: runHTTP in the member calls fetch with no signal, runAI awaits env.AI.run with no deadline, runTick runs every due fleet_crons task in sequence and moves next_fire only after the task returns (a stuck task keeps its cron due), and five fleet_runs rows have stood queued or running since 10-23 to 10-25 (report-card-weekly running since 2026-10-24T13:36Z).' || char(10) ||
  'FIX (qnfo-code-orchestrator/worker.js only): bound every promise the scheduled handler waits on so no invocation can outlive a deadline, and say which step was pending: (1) a helper withDeadline(promise, ms, label) that settles with the promise or, at the deadline, writes one cloud_ops_events row code-task.scheduled-deadline naming the label and resolves; (2) wrap the runFleetExecMember call and the main tick promise in scheduled() with it at 240000 ms; (3) give runHTTP an AbortSignal.timeout of 25000 ms and wrap runAI with the helper at 120000 ms; (4) mark a fleet_runs row failed with the deadline text instead of leaving it running. VERSION: a minor bump (capability: deadline guard).' || char(10) ||
  'Definition of done: no scheduled invocation of qnfo-code-orchestrator runs over 600 seconds in the 24 hours after the deploy (the probe on this issue), and the code-task.scheduled-deadline events name the step that stalled, which is the input of the next fix.' || char(10) ||
  'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-code-orchestrator/worker.js' || char(10) ||
  'code-anchor: async function runFleetExecMember(event, env) {',
  'claude-session:rem-a7', 'ops', 'high', 'open',
  CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'CODE-ORCH-WALL-STALL-1:%' AND status = 'open');

INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT
  'EMAIL-OWNER-CODE-VIOLATION-NOISE-1: all 22 unresolved consent-violation rows are the owner''s own sign-in code mails, so a real violation would hide among them',
  'Charter pillar: security. Found in the security and compliance review of owner task 1000068, measured 2026-10-26 in qnfo-audit.email_send_violations.' || char(10) ||
  'FINDING: the 22 unresolved rows (2026-10-20 to 2026-10-25, type UNGATED-SEND-TO-SUPPRESSED-OR-REPEAT) are all mails with the subject "Owner code" and a six digit number, one recipient, system sender qnfo@qnfo.org: the owner''s sign-in code (qnfo-ops sends it through qnfo-email with handoff true). The trigger emails_outbound_violation_detect flags every emails row with status sent or replied whose recipient has reply_count above 0 or suppress 1 in contact_ledger, and the owner is in the ledger. A real send to a suppressed or already-replied recipient would be one more row in a list that already reads 22.' || char(10) ||
  'FIX (qnfo-email/worker.js only; the detector stays as it is, it is a consent guard and is not weakened): the send path (sendApi and where it stores the sent row) records a mail sent with handoff true (owner-directed transactional mail) under its own status, sent-handoff, instead of sent, so the detector does not read it and nothing else that reads emails.status = sent changes for outreach, replies or digests. The 22 existing rows are left for the detector''s owner to resolve once the new status is live.' || char(10) ||
  'Definition of done: no new violation row with the subject Owner code in 7 days (the probe on this issue); the detector trigger text is unchanged.' || char(10) ||
  'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-email/worker.js' || char(10) ||
  'code-anchor: async function sendApi(req,e,J){',
  'claude-session:rem-a7', 'ops', 'medium', 'open',
  CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'EMAIL-OWNER-CODE-VIOLATION-NOISE-1:%' AND status = 'open');

UPDATE remediation_contracts
   SET verify_transport = 'code-read', verify_probe = '{"paths": ["qnfo-fleet-control/worker.js"], "contains": "ai_spend_owner_client"}',
       status = 'active', module = 'rem-a7-owner-v1', attempts = 0, last_verdict = NULL, next_due_at = datetime('now', '+120 minutes'), expected_cadence_h = 1, max_attempts = 3,
       precondition = 'the code-probe line of the issue (OWNER-LOCAL-CLIENT-TAG-1), set by REM-A7-OWNER-B-1 because the birth template replaces the probe-line contract',
       action = 'the doer teaches olClassify and ownerLocalIngest in qnfo-fleet-control/worker.js the owner_client metadata key and writes ai_spend_owner_client; scripts/remediation_consumer.py reads worker.js on main every hour and a pass closes the issue. It reads fail today (the worker never mentions ai_spend_owner_client).'
 WHERE class = 'issue-' || (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'OWNER-LOCAL-CLIENT-TAG-1:%' AND status = 'open' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1)
   AND status = 'superseded' AND instr(verify_probe, 'SELECT ''closed'' AS expected') = 1;

UPDATE remediation_contracts
   SET verify_transport = 'd1-query',
       verify_probe = 'SELECT ''0'' AS expected, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM worker_logs WHERE script_name = ''qnfo-code-orchestrator'' AND event_type = ''telemetry:scheduled'' AND outcome IN (''exceededWallTime'', ''canceled'') AND wall_ms > 600000 AND ts_ms > (strftime(''%s'', ''now'') - 86400) * 1000) AS TEXT) AS observed',
       status = 'active', module = 'rem-a7-owner-v1', attempts = 0, last_verdict = NULL, next_due_at = datetime('now', '+120 minutes'), expected_cadence_h = 1, max_attempts = 3,
       precondition = 'qnfo-observability ingests Logpush failures of qnfo-code-orchestrator into worker_logs (13 stalled scheduled invocations in the 24 hours before this file)',
       action = 'the doer adds the deadline guard of the issue to qnfo-code-orchestrator/worker.js; the probe counts scheduled invocations over 600 seconds in the last 24 hours and reads 0 only after the deploy has held a day. It reads 13 before the fix.'
 WHERE class = 'issue-' || (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'CODE-ORCH-WALL-STALL-1:%' AND status = 'open' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1)
   AND status = 'superseded' AND instr(verify_probe, 'SELECT ''closed'' AS expected') = 1;

UPDATE remediation_contracts
   SET verify_transport = 'd1-query',
       verify_probe = 'SELECT ''0'' AS expected, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM email_send_violations WHERE violation = ''UNGATED-SEND-TO-SUPPRESSED-OR-REPEAT'' AND subject LIKE ''Owner code %'' AND detected_at >= datetime(''now'', ''-7 days'')) AS TEXT) AS observed',
       status = 'active', module = 'rem-a7-owner-v1', attempts = 0, last_verdict = NULL, next_due_at = datetime('now', '+120 minutes'), expected_cadence_h = 1, max_attempts = 3,
       precondition = 'emails_outbound_violation_detect is unchanged and qnfo-email records owner-directed handoff mail under the status sent-handoff once the fix is live',
       action = 'the doer changes sendApi in qnfo-email/worker.js; the probe counts consent-violation rows for Owner code mail in the last 7 days and reads 0 once no new one is written for a week. It reads 22 before the fix (6 days of rows).'
 WHERE class = 'issue-' || (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'EMAIL-OWNER-CODE-VIOLATION-NOISE-1:%' AND status = 'open' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1)
   AND status = 'superseded' AND instr(verify_probe, 'SELECT ''closed'' AS expected') = 1;

INSERT INTO human_actions (slug, title, why, default_in_effect, action, url, sev, status, source, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'tag-owner-desktop-clients',
  'Tag your desktop AI clients so their spend is attributed per client',
  'IDENTITY-BOUND: the settings are on your own machines; the fleet cannot reach them. Measured 2026-10-26: 242.43 USD of list cost in 30 days (opus-5.5 177.57, sonnet-5.5 33.05, deepseek-flash 23.17, deepseek-v4-pro 8.64) comes from untagged desktop clients on the stored provider keys; every request carries user_agent node, your gateway token and no tag, so the fleet cannot say which client spent what (agent_issues 100384 and 100406 are answered with that breakdown). The fleet tag (worker or caller) must not be used: it would move the spend into the fleet caps. The fleet side is agent_issues OWNER-LOCAL-CLIENT-TAG-1: it teaches the cost ingest a separate key, owner_client, and writes a per-client table.',
  'The spend keeps being attributed as untagged owner-local cost: visible in the all-in view, excluded from the fleet caps, not split by client. Nothing is blocked.',
  'Once the fleet side has landed (the issue OWNER-LOCAL-CLIENT-TAG-1 is closed), add one custom request header to each desktop client that calls the AI Gateway: name cf-aig-metadata, value {"owner_client":"<a short name for that client>"} (for example a different name for each coding agent and each chat client). Most clients that speak the chat-completions or the messages API format have a custom headers setting; a client without one stays untagged. The step is done when the cost page shows per-client rows: SELECT client, SUM(usd) FROM ai_spend_owner_client GROUP BY client reads one row for each tagged client.',
  'https://fleet.qnfo.org/', 'normal', 'open', 'session:rem-a7', datetime('now'), datetime('now')
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM human_actions WHERE slug = 'tag-owner-desktop-clients');

UPDATE human_actions
   SET status = 'open', resolved_at = NULL, resolution = NULL, updated_at = datetime('now')
 WHERE slug IN ('tag-owner-desktop-clients', 'attest-first-credibility-event') AND status = 'resolved' AND source = 'session:rem-a7' AND instr(COALESCE(resolution, ''), 'DEFAULT-ADOPTED-1') = 1;

INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence)
SELECT a.id, 'rem-a7-owner-b', 'closed', 'rem-a7', datetime('now'),
  'Attribution delivered, measured 2026-10-26 (rem-a7). Untagged owner-local spend is qnfo-audit.ai_spend_owner_local (gateway default, list cost of requests that carry no worker or caller tag, COST-OWNER-SPLIT-1): 242.43 USD over the last 30 days (it was 167.31 when the task was filed on 10-20; about 75.1 USD since: claude-opus-5.5 on 10-21 58.57, deepseek on 10-24 and 10-25 16.54). By model: claude-opus-5.5 177.57 USD (1,802 calls on 3 days: 10-17, 10-18, 10-21), claude-sonnet-5.5 33.05 (662 calls, 10-17), deepseek-flash 23.17 (8,195 calls on 8 days), deepseek-v4-pro 8.64 (1,111 calls on 5 days), claude-sonnet-4.5 0.00 (1 call); no Anthropic call after 2026-10-21. Which clients: the gateway log of those requests was read with the allowlisted non-content action (cf-ops-actions gateway-logs, runs 40383249752 for claude-opus-5.5 and 40383253899 for deepseek-flash, 2026-10-26T19:04Z, the newest 300 rows of each): every row has user_agent node, authentication true (the account''s gateway token was presented), byok alias default (the stored provider key) and metadata none. The claude-opus-5.5 rows are the native /v1/messages path, prompt tokens median 2 (cache-dominated), output median 767 and p90 5,456, 9.6 s median, 10:34Z to 14:45Z on 10-21: the shape of an interactive coding-agent session. The deepseek-flash rows are /chat/completions, 297 of 300 inside one hour on 10-25 (11:44Z to 13:09Z), prompt tokens median 208,238 and p90 387,112, output median 789: the shape of an agent loop re-sending a context of about 200,000 tokens. Who owns them: the key is the Cloudflare account''s own stored provider key behind the default gateway and every call presented the account''s gateway token, so the account is the owner''s and the person is the owner (single-owner fleet); the card tag-owner-desktop-clients records that nothing else holds that token. Per client: not separable. All the requests identify as one user agent with no tag, so two clients of one person cannot be told apart and the 30 day cost by client stays unknown until the clients tag themselves. Tagging, as asked, would do harm: olClassify in qnfo-fleet-control takes any request with metadata worker or caller as fleet spend (ai_spend_ledger, counted against ai_spend:anthropic cap 15 and ai_spend:total cap 150), and one gateway per client is ruled out by fleet_budget ai_gateways cap 1. What was built: the successor issue ' || COALESCE((SELECT CAST(MAX(id) AS TEXT) FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'OWNER-LOCAL-CLIENT-TAG-1:%'), '?') || ' (OWNER-LOCAL-CLIENT-TAG-1: qnfo-fleet-control learns the key owner_client, code task with the anchor verified once on main, closing probe a code-read that fails today), the table ai_spend_owner_client, and the IDENTITY-BOUND card tag-owner-desktop-clients for the settings on his machines.'
FROM agent_issues a
WHERE a.id = 100384 AND a.status = 'open'
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN ('active', 'holding') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict, '') IN ('fail', 'vacuous-probe-result', 'probe-error', 'probe-not-machine-executable', 'probe-same-account-host'))
ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = 'closed', owner = excluded.owner, close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence;

INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence)
SELECT a.id, 'rem-a7-owner-b', 'closed', 'rem-a7', datetime('now'),
  'Audit delivered (rem-a7, 2026-10-26); the measurements and the client identification are in the close evidence of issue 100384 (same reading of ai_spend_owner_local and of the gateway log). Clients, models, 30 day list cost, in order: Node-user-agent coding agent on claude-opus-5.5, 177.57 USD, 1,802 calls, 3 days (10-17, 10-18, 10-21); the same client class on claude-sonnet-5.5, 33.05 USD, 662 calls, 10-17; a Node-user-agent agent loop on deepseek-flash, 23.17 USD, 8,195 calls, 8 days; the same class on deepseek-v4-pro, 8.64 USD, 1,111 calls, 5 days; total 242.43 USD. Per call: opus 0.0985, sonnet-5.5 0.0499, deepseek-v4-pro 0.0078, deepseek-flash 0.0028 USD. Tag or retire: tag, once the fleet side exists (a client cannot be retired that cannot be told apart from another; the card tag-owner-desktop-clients carries the step that is yours). Recommendation for 300 USD all-in, with the evidence each part rests on. The cap cannot be met by trimming owner-local spend alone: v_cost_forecast on 2026-10-26 reads the fleet scope at a 30 day pace of 289.48 USD against its budget of 300 (forecast for the month 362.33), the owner_clients scope at 165.41 (forecast 260.96, no budget) and owner_direct_unverified, the owner-stated provider subscriptions that no API sees, at 450 (basis column: UNVERIFIED): about 905 USD in 30 days against 300, and metric monthly_cost_run_rate_usd reads 1,466.84 against 580. The fleet scope alone is at 96 percent of 300 before anything else counts, and fleet_budget cost:fleet_all_in_month (cap 300, current 289.48) meters that scope only; owner-local spend is excluded from it on purpose (COST-OWNER-SPLIT-1). So the owner has one decision to name: whether all-in 300 means the fleet scope (within) or fleet plus owner clients plus direct providers (about 905). Levers by size: (1) the 450 USD of direct providers is half of the all-in figure and cannot be verified from here (only the provider invoices say; the owner''s own financial data); (2) owner-local Anthropic is 210.62 of the 242.43 (87 percent) and came from three days of claude-opus-5.5 coding sessions at about twice the per-call cost of claude-sonnet-5.5 and about 35 times deepseek-flash: routing routine turns to the cheaper tiers is the lever; whether it keeps output quality cannot be read from billing data (no per-route quality measure exists for these clients), so it is a recommendation, not a measured result; (3) the DeepSeek loop that sent prompts of about 208,000 tokens 3,919 times on 10-25 cost 13.73 USD of the 15.88 that day in about 85 minutes: a lean context or prefix caching is the lever for that class of loop (how often it runs is not known: DeepSeek spend appears on 8 of the last 30 days). The fleet scope is held by the cost loops (COST-SUSTAIN-1, the breach doctor), not by this task.'
FROM agent_issues a
WHERE a.id = 100406 AND a.status = 'open'
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN ('active', 'holding') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict, '') IN ('fail', 'vacuous-probe-result', 'probe-error', 'probe-not-machine-executable', 'probe-same-account-host'))
ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = 'closed', owner = excluded.owner, close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence;

INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence)
SELECT a.id, 'rem-a7-owner-b', 'closed', 'rem-a7', datetime('now'),
  'Five items, each with a disposition measured on 2026-10-26 (rem-a7). 1 GATE-FLAKE-RATE: resolved. Issue 1000055 (closed with evidence) measured the worker load gate step at 0 failures in 99 of the last 100 completed deploy-gate runs (2026-10-26T04:46Z to 07:52Z), step duration 1 to 4 s, so no entry waits out the 20 s timeout. 2 CI-ZERO-RUNS: resolved. deploy-gate.yml has runs (the last 100: 71 success, 10 failure, 6 cancelled, 13 in progress at 19:15Z) and model-floor-guard.yml ran at 19:11Z, 19:12Z and 19:15Z, all success. 3 BREACH-TRIAGE: per owner now, from v_metric_trigger_state with hit 1: 63 breaches, qnfo-fleet-control 37 (59 percent, mixed ratio and count metrics from 0.02 to 1,466.84, so 37 is a count of metrics, not of incidents), program-manager:QNFO.OPS 6, qnfo-research-exec 4, qnfo-code-orchestrator 4, qnfo-ops 3, q08-signal-engine 3, qnfo-social 2, and one each for qnfo-lifecycle, qnfo-kaizen, qnfo-github-steward and idea-hub; the per-metric triage is the breach doctor (docs/breach-doctor/FAMILY-METRIC-CLASSIFICATION.md, BREACH-DOCTOR-1 code tasks queued), which owns closing them. 4 COST-DENOMINATOR: explained. v_cost_forecast has budget_month_usd 300 for the fleet scope (owner directive 2026-10-21, all-in, migrations/2026-10-21-cost-sustain-forecast.sql) and null for the two owner scopes by design; the pace of 450 USD is the owner_direct_unverified scope, labelled UNVERIFIED in its basis column (the owner-stated monthly figure divided by 30, which no API sees); the fleet denominator is verified, the owner-direct one can only be verified from the provider invoices. 5 HUMAN-WAIT-SOURCE: pinned. human_wait_oldest_min is written by qnfo-fleet-dashboard (worker.js, upd(''human_wait_oldest_min'', round(oldest_days x 1440))) from the dashboard attention view, which counts code_tasks in status needs_human plus open human_actions (docs/breach-doctor/FAMILY-METRIC.md names the needs_human code tasks as its source and notes that human_actions held no open row); it reads 21 minutes now against a target of 120, from 18,329 when filed.'
FROM agent_issues a
WHERE a.id = 1000063 AND a.status = 'open'
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN ('active', 'holding') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict, '') IN ('fail', 'vacuous-probe-result', 'probe-error', 'probe-not-machine-executable', 'probe-same-account-host'))
ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = 'closed', owner = excluded.owner, close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence;

INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence)
SELECT a.id, 'rem-a7-owner-b', 'closed', 'rem-a7', datetime('now'),
  'Review of the research and content area (qnfo-ops, personal-api, ideas.qnfo.org, qnfo.org, papers.qnfo.org), rem-a7, 2026-10-26. Method and limits: reads of qnfo-audit (email_send_violations, contact_ledger, email_reply_queue, outreach_queue, workers_bp_findings, the BP26 issue set), of the code paths named, and one unauthenticated request per host (a header read of the front page, a key check on the key-gated routes, one 1-token chat request); no scan, no secret read, no change. RANKED FINDINGS. 1 HIGH, realised harm, identity: outbound mail in the owner''s name with no owner in the loop. email_reply_queue 75 and 76 are tier 2, decision sent, to one external recipient of the fleet''s own outreach; 76 (sent 2026-10-22T18:15:55Z) answered a complaint in the owner''s voice and drew a sharper one (he took the notes for spam and the replies for an incompetent AI agent). Cause: tier 2 is one model verdict with no owner switch and no rule for a recipient of the fleet''s own mail. Smallest effective fix: tier 2 keeps its auto-send marker only while ops_config email_tier2_autosend is on (absent means off: the row goes to the owner with its draft), plus a rule that recipients of outreach and complaint wording go to the owner. Owner and doer: qnfo-email, issue 1000469 (open, code-task line on qnfo-email/worker.js, probe: the switch exists on main, fails today). A reply draft for the owner is stored under issue 1000101. 2 HIGH, compliance exposure, no incident yet: EU AI Act Article 50 labelling and provenance of AI-generated public content (q08, reading.q08.org, papers, social posts), issues 1000341 (visible labels, first-interaction disclosure) and 1000335 (machine-readable marking), both critical, open, programme-owned (QNFO.OPS and QNFO.RSCH), contracts failing because the gap exists; and 1000359, prompt-injection and goal-hijack defences for the mail-reading agent (critical, open; qnfo-email 2.12.0 merged, 2.12.1 in PR 4801). These are the catalogued large items; no duplicate is filed. 3 MEDIUM, control quality: the consent-violation ledger cannot show a real violation. All 22 unresolved email_send_violations rows (2026-10-20 to 10-25, UNGATED-SEND-TO-SUPPRESSED-OR-REPEAT) are the owner''s own sign-in code mails (subject Owner code and six digits, one recipient, system sender); the trigger emails_outbound_violation_detect flags any sent row whose recipient has reply_count above 0 in contact_ledger and the owner is in the ledger, so a real send to a suppressed address would hide in a list that already reads 22. Fix kept narrow so the detector is not weakened: qnfo-email records owner-directed handoff mail under its own status. Owner and doer: qnfo-email, issue ' || COALESCE((SELECT CAST(MAX(id) AS TEXT) FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'EMAIL-OWNER-CODE-VIOLATION-NOISE-1:%'), '?') || ' (new; probe: no new Owner code row in 7 days, reads 22 now). 4 MEDIUM, edge baseline: header read of the front pages on 2026-10-26: qnfo.org sends HSTS with preload, nosniff, Referrer-Policy and Permissions-Policy but no X-Frame-Options and no Content-Security-Policy; papers.qnfo.org, ideas.qnfo.org and ops.qnfo.org add X-Frame-Options DENY and still send no Content-Security-Policy; me.q08.org (the personal host) sends only HSTS (no preload) and nosniff. Owner: BP26-EDGE-SECURITY-1 (issue 1000356, open, high). 5 LOW, documentation drift: docs/keys/owner-api-keys.md (read 2026-10-05) says ai.qnfo.org answers 401 without a key; on 2026-10-26 a keyless chat request to ai.qnfo.org answers 200 with the header x-ops-access public-read, the same public read mode ops.qnfo.org documents; that is consistent with OPEN-ACCESS-1 only if the per-visitor and global caps hold, which this review did not test (one 1-token request). me.q08.org answers 401 to a keyless chat request, ideas.qnfo.org answers 401 to a keyless intake and fleet.qnfo.org/api/owner/keys answers 403, as designed. 6 LOW, already owned: 18 advisory workers_bp_findings on these workers (qnfo-gateway 6, personal-api 4, idea-hub 3, qnfo-ai-search 3, qnfo-ops 1, qnfo-subscribers 1; none above advisory) and the privacy and retention items 1000342 to 1000344 under BP26. CHECKED, NO VIOLATION FOUND: subscribers_with_consent_proof reads 1 (the one confirmed subscriber has its consent timestamp); outreach_queue 193 rows with every send in a terminal status and the learner stop rule holding segment other:institutional (53 sends, no positive reply, stopped 2026-10-21); papers.qnfo.org answers 404 for quarantined slugs, unknown slugs and unknown snapshots (the evidence of issue 100575). NOT DONE, and why: active probing of the five hosts, a review of secret storage and rotation state (secret lock) and a legal reading of Article 50 need the owner or the programme owners.'
FROM agent_issues a
WHERE a.id = 1000068 AND a.status = 'open'
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN ('active', 'holding') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict, '') IN ('fail', 'vacuous-probe-result', 'probe-error', 'probe-not-machine-executable', 'probe-same-account-host'))
ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = 'closed', owner = excluded.owner, close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence;

INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence)
SELECT a.id, 'rem-a7-owner-b', 'closed', 'rem-a7', datetime('now'),
  'Diagnosed to the class and handed over, superseded by CODE-ORCH-WALL-STALL-1 (issue ' || COALESCE((SELECT CAST(MAX(id) AS TEXT) FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'CODE-ORCH-WALL-STALL-1:%'), '?') || ', open, high, doer the code loop through its code-task line on qnfo-code-orchestrator/worker.js with a code anchor that occurs once on main, probe a d1-query on worker_logs that reads 13 now). Measured 2026-10-26 (rem-a7). The owner''s three events in 24 hours are the Cloudflare census figure (worker_usage_daily errors_24h: 4 of 1,366 requests on 10-24, 2 of 1,488 on 10-25, 6 of 1,869 on 10-26) and match the platform codes 3046 Request timeout and 5030 in worker_logs outcome exception (120 rows in 7 days, each event logged twice, no cpu or wall time): platform-side, not thrown by this code. The worker-owned failure is larger and different: in the last 24 hours 13 scheduled invocations, and in 7 days 71, ran 899.7 to 900.0 seconds of wall time with at most 200 ms of CPU and ended canceled or exceededWallTime, which means the handler awaited something that never returned. It does not track a deploy (0.28.0 went live 2026-10-26T06:24Z, stalls at 06:37, 06:57, 16:03, 16:53, 16:59). Candidates read in worker.js on main: scheduled() awaits the folded fleet-exec member and hands the main tick to waitUntil; runHTTP fetches with no signal, runAI awaits env.AI.run with no deadline, runTick runs every due fleet_crons task in sequence and moves next_fire only after the task returns, and five fleet_runs rows stand queued or running since 10-23 to 10-25. Not proven: which await stalls. The successor''s first lever bounds every wait and logs which step was pending, which is the input of the next fix; a fix of the root cause is not claimed here.'
FROM agent_issues a
WHERE a.id = 1000079 AND a.status = 'open'
  AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues s WHERE s.title LIKE 'CODE-ORCH-WALL-STALL-1:%' AND s.status = 'open')
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN ('active', 'holding') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict, '') IN ('fail', 'vacuous-probe-result', 'probe-error', 'probe-not-machine-executable', 'probe-same-account-host'))
ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = 'closed', owner = excluded.owner, close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence;

